# Local WSL Auto-Validation

After every turn that edits `lib/**`, `test/**`, `web/**`, `docker/**`, `pubspec.yaml`, or `assets/data/**`, **run validation in WSL** before marking work complete.

## Command matrix

| Trigger | WSL commands |
|---------|----------------|
| Any code/data change | `flutter pub get && flutter analyze && flutter test` |
| UI, routing, or feature slice | + `bash scripts/wsl_dev.sh` (background); smoke `http://localhost:3000/` |
| docker/nginx/pubspec/deploy | Tier 2: `bash scripts/wsl_deploy.sh`; verify `/` and `/session/s-001` refresh |
| End of plan run / before push | Tier 1 green **and** Tier 2 green **and** coverage gate green |

Windows host prefix: `wsl -e bash -lc 'cd /mnt/c/NAGP/flo-compass && <cmd>'`

## On pass or fail

1. **Fix blockers** in the same turn when feasible (analyze errors, failing tests, 404 deep links).
2. Report Tier 1/2 status and smoke notes when closing the turn.

## Skip validation only when

- Read-only Q&A with zero file edits
- Pure docs prose with no code/data impact

## Do not

- Claim a plan run is done without final Tier 1 at minimum
- Skip Tier 2 after docker/nginx/routing changes or before push
- Run `flutter`/`docker` from PowerShell as the primary workflow

---

## Tier reference

**Tier 1 & Tier 2** run inside WSL2 for local testing. Open URLs from the Windows browser at `http://localhost:<port>`.

**Tier 3 (production):** GitHub Actions builds the Docker image, pushes to GHCR, and deploys to Fly.io. WSL is not part of the production deploy path.

### Tier 1 — Flutter dev (every UI change, WSL)

```bash
flutter pub get && flutter analyze && flutter test && dart format --set-exit-if-changed .
flutter run -d web-server --web-port=3000 --web-hostname=0.0.0.0
# Or: bash scripts/wsl_dev.sh
# Verify http://localhost:3000/
```

### Tier 2 — Docker local smoke (before every push to default, WSL)

```bash
docker compose up --build
# Or: bash scripts/wsl_deploy.sh
# Verify http://localhost:8080/ AND http://localhost:8080/session/s-001 (deep link refresh)
```

### Tier 3 — Fly.io (production — after push to default branch)

- Triggered by `.github/workflows/ci-deploy.yml` on default-branch push
- Image: `ghcr.io/<owner>/<repo>:<sha>` with `CONFIG_PROFILE=prod`
- Confirm workflow summary: `Deployed to https://{app}.fly.dev`
- Deep-link test: hit `https://{app}.fly.dev/session/s-001` directly (browser refresh) — must NOT 404

### Parity rule

What works in Tier 1 must work in Tier 2. Tier 3 uses the **same `docker/Dockerfile` image** — WSL Tier 2 validates that image locally before push.
